{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Jmvr9oK4KdmAerEDyo5fTA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The `cancellation` service is implemented and all tests pass.\n\n## What I found and did\n\nThe scaffold and the v1 implementation already existed, but the code was **v1-only** — it refunded money but didn't return the room to inventory. The pre-written tests (`server_v2_test.go`) require the v2 behavior. I closed that gap:\n\n**`internal/server/server.go`** — added the inventory dependency:\n- New `NewServerWithInventory(booking, payment, inventory)` constructor (v2), while keeping `NewServer(booking, payment)` valid (v1) so the frozen v1 test file keeps passing.\n- `Cancel` now runs two reversals in fixed order: `payment.Refund(auth_id, amount)`, then `inventory.ReturnStock(hotel_id, room_type, date, 1)`. A refund failure short-circuits before inventory is touched; a `ReturnStock` failure surfaces as `FailedPrecondition` with no compensation (refund stays applied) — exactly matching the SPEC and the v2 tests. When `inventory` is nil (v1 constructor) the return step is skipped.\n\n**`cmd/cancellation/main.go`** — dials the `inventory` upstream (`INVENTORY_ADDR`, default `inventory:50051`) and wires it via `NewServerWithInventory`.\n\n**`Dockerfile`** — copies `services/inventory` and adds it to the inline `go.work`.\n\nVerified `go.mod` has no cross-service `require`/`replace` (workspace resolves them).\n\n## Verification\n- `go build ./services/cancellation/...` → clean\n- `go test ./services/cancellation/...` → `ok` (all 7 tests: v1 happy/empty/not-found/refund-fail + v2 returns-and-refunds/refund-fail-no-return/return-stock-fails)\n\n## One thing to flag (not in my scope)\nThe repo's `go.work` lists `./tests/integration`, but that directory has no `go.mod` (it doesn't exist), so a plain `go build ./...` from the repo root fails for **every** service, not just this one:\n\n```\ngo: cannot load module ../../tests/integration listed in go.work file:\nopen ../../tests/integration/go.mod: no such file or directory\n```\n\nI worked around it for verification with a temporary workspace rather than edit the framework-managed `go.work`. You'll likely want either to create `tests/integration/go.mod` or drop that entry from `go.work` so `make build`/`make test` work as written."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":314,"cache_read_input_tokens":45544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":314},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"504cdaaf-3d18-4ab0-8bd7-ba7867ec0a8b","uuid":"f93e968c-5559-4bbe-8b0e-59617e6e5a02","request_id":"req_011CboGGHbxkPMx43b5EJiiY"}
